//!
//! # Drivers
//!
//! The devices the kernel talks to directly: the COM1 serial port, the
//! framebuffer text console with its font, and the PS/2 keyboard.
//!
//! ## Public API
//!
//! | Name                | File            | Purpose                                                  |
//! |---------------------|-----------------|----------------------------------------------------------|
//! | `Drivers::Serial`   | `serial.ign`    | COM1 output, the kernel's first and last-resort log      |
//! | `Drivers::Console`  | `console.ign`   | framebuffer text console that mirrors every byte to COM1 |
//! | `Drivers::Color`    | `console.ign`   | the 16 palette indices                                   |
//! | `Drivers::Font`     | `font.ign`      | glyph lookup in the 8x16 bitmap font                     |
//! | `Drivers::FontData` | `font_8x16.ign` | the generated glyph table (`make font`)                  |
//! | `Drivers::Ps2`      | `ps2.ign`       | 8042 controller setup and the IRQ1 handler               |
//! | `Drivers::Keyboard` | `keyboard.ign`  | scancode set 1 to ASCII decoding                         |
//!
//! ## Dependencies
//!
//! | Imports | Why                                                       |
//! |---------|-----------------------------------------------------------|
//! | `Arch`  | port I/O, interrupt flag handling                         |
//! | `Lib`   | integer formatting, `memmove`, the scancode ring buffer   |
//! | `Boot`  | `Console::initialize` takes the Limine framebuffer record |
//!
//! Every other subsystem may import `Drivers` to print. `Drivers` imports
//! nothing above `Boot`.

import _ from "./console";
import _ from "./font";
import _ from "./keyboard";
import _ from "./ps2";
import _ from "./serial";

/// Aggregate namespace of the device drivers. The files above contribute the
/// sub-namespaces listed in the module header.
export namespace Drivers {}
